      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am sending our AI review:\n\nOverall approach and speedup (~3×) on large ref sets are great, but the parallel ACL evaluation in ReadAccessClassifier introduces a few critical correctness and security discrepancies compared to Gerrit\u0027s authoritative PermissionCollection / RefControl semantics:\n\n1. Security / ACL Bypass in Multi-Level Inheritance (ReadAccessClassifier.java:137-142):\n`exclusiveMatchers` only tracks `ownProject`. If an intermediate parent project in a hierarchy (Child -\u003e Parent -\u003e All-Projects) defines an exclusive READ section to suppress parent allows, it is ignored by `exclusiveMatchers`. Grandparent allow rules (e.g. ALLOW READ refs/* in All-Projects) then match, leaking protected refs in child repositories.\n\n2. Incorrect DENY Action Semantics (ReadAccessClassifier.java:166-170):\nIn Gerrit (PermissionCollection.calculateAllowRules), DENY is a group-specific shadowing rule (shadowing inherited ALLOW rules for that same group), not an absolute BLOCK. Treating DENY as an immediate INVISIBLE veto incorrectly blocks users who belong to multiple groups (e.g. Contractors with DENY and Registered Users with ALLOW).\n\n3. In-Project Exclusive ALLOW vs BLOCK Precedence (ReadAccessClassifier.java:87-91):\nIn Gerrit, an exclusive ALLOW on a specific pattern overrides a BLOCK in the same project. In ReadAccessClassifier, `denyMatchers` is evaluated first, returning INVISIBLE before allowMatchers is checked.\n\nArchitectural Suggestion:\nRather than implementing a parallel ACL engine covering complex ACL corner cases, consider a safe short-circuit strategy:\n- Fast-path pre-compiled classifier: Pre-compile and short-circuit when the project hierarchy contains no BLOCK, no DENY, and no exclusive rules (which covers the vast majority of repos).\n- Graceful fallback: If any exclusive, BLOCK, or DENY rules exist for READ in the hierarchy, return NEEDS_FULL_CHECK and delegate to the existing PermissionCollection / RefControl.\n\nSee inline comments for details on individual files.",
