      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T11:40:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Critical: Exclusive READ permissions in intermediate parent projects are bypassed\n\ncompileRules() only populates exclusiveMatchers for the immediate project (isOwnSection):\n```java\nboolean isOwnSection \u003d sectionMatcher.getProject().equals(ownProject);\nif (isOwnSection \u0026\u0026 readPermission.getExclusiveGroup()) {\n  exclusiveMatchers.add(sectionMatcher);\n}\n```\nIn a multi-level hierarchy (ChildRepo -\u003e ParentRepo -\u003e All-Projects):\n1. ParentRepo defines an exclusive READ rule on refs/heads/secret/* (to suppress All-Projects\u0027s ALLOW READ refs/* for Registered Users).\n2. When evaluating ChildRepo, ParentRepo is not ownProject.\n3. exclusiveMatchers remains empty for refs/heads/secret/*.\n4. In classify(), coveredByExclusiveSection is false, and parentAllowMatchers (which contains All-Projects\u0027s refs/*) matches and returns Decision.VISIBLE.\n\nThis bypasses the parent\u0027s exclusive permission and leaks protected refs in child repositories.\n\nTo fix this, ReadAccessClassifier must either track exclusivity per ancestor level in hierarchy order, or return NEEDS_FULL_CHECK whenever any project in the inheritance chain contains an exclusive permission section.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 142,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
