      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T11:40:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correctness: DENY action is treated as a global BLOCK\n\nIn Gerrit (PermissionCollection.calculateAllowRules), DENY only shadows ALLOW rules for the same group on inherited/less specific sections (via SeenRule(refPattern, group)). It does not act as a universal block for all groups the user belongs to.\n\nExample:\n- All-Projects has ALLOW READ refs/* for Registered Users.\n- A child project has DENY READ refs/heads/* for External-Contractors.\n- Alice belongs to both Registered Users and External-Contractors.\n\nIn Gerrit, Alice can read refs/heads/main because Registered Users grants access and DENY only shadows External-Contractors. In ReadAccessClassifier, refs/heads/* is placed into denyMatchers and immediately returns Decision.INVISIBLE.\n\nIf a section contains a matching DENY rule, the classifier should either return NEEDS_FULL_CHECK or implement full group-aware SeenRule deduplication.",
